{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1118852-how-is-the-probability-for-fate-conditional-duration-evaluated","id":1118852,"title":"How is the probability for (Fate: Conditional Duration) evaluated?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-20T23:59:58-07:00","id":1118852,"title":"How is the probability for (Fate: Conditional Duration) evaluated?","content":"On page 192 of the 2nd ed. corebook, the Conditional Duration attainment refers to common, infrequent, and improbable for evaluating the bonus to duration. What is the probability relative to? Does the attainment do a bit of meta-gaming with respect to previous behavior, present circumstance, or future intentions?<br /> <br /> If I say, &quot;This spell goes off if I am about to die.&quot; does the spell check for how often I've been near death before (aka you've been there many times before, so you'll probably be there again - common)? Or does it check for the probability of being close to death with my current plans (aka about to go face the big bad and his crew)? Or does it look at the immediate circumstance and say &quot;You are currently not dying, and without help from external factors you will not be near-dying any time soon - improbable.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it may be the last example (checking immediate circumstance), but then it seems the attainment does exercise a bit of meta-gaming by checking on the likelihood that you snap a glass rod for the express purpose of releasing a spell.<br /> <br /> Clarity on this matter would be greatly appreciated.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T02:21:14-07:00","id":1118872,"title":"","content":"Think its ST fiat territory here. You just have to come up with what sounds the best between your group. If you cast the &quot;goes off if i am about to die&quot; before doing something suicidal then its probably common, if you cast it and then hide in a bunker like a hermit then its probably improbable. I think the attainment will have some metagame knowledge (ie the ST will probably know) and give its bonus based on what he thinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T03:58:07-07:00","id":1118895,"title":"","content":"Considering it's a Fate attainment I think it's reasonable to assume it has some &quot;understanding&quot; of the probability of an event relative to your situation and intent. It would be kind of dumb, for example, if it treated the condition &quot;I walk past another person&quot; the same on the streets of Tokyo and in the middle of the Sahara. As for the glass rod, I'd say that something that won't happen unless someone goes out of their way to make it happen automatically qualifies as at least &quot;infrequent&quot; regardless of intent.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I just want to point out that Conditional Duration doesn't make a spell &quot;go off&quot; unless you use Hung Spell (Time 2). It makes the spell <i>turn</i> off.<br /> <br /> And on an even sider note, I'd personally ask for something a little more exact than &quot;about to die&quot;, just because I'd have a hard time arbitrating that. Are you &quot;about to die&quot; if you're hanging off a ledge? If someone throws a grenade that risks killing you, are you &quot;about to die&quot; when you take the damage, when the grenade explodes but before you're damaged, when it's thrown or even when the enemy makes the decision to throw a grenade? If you're infiltrating an enemy compound at great personal risk are you constantly about to die? I'd much prefer something like &quot;when targeted by an attack&quot; or &quot;when my health track is full&quot;.<br /> <br /> e: in fact, the Attainment itself specifies that &quot;improbable&quot; means &quot;unlikely to happen <b>given current conditions</b>&quot;, and it has something similar to say about &quot;common&quot; meaning something that will &quot;almost certainly happen <b>in the near future</b>&quot;. That pretty explicitly says that the attainment cares about how likely things are based on the circumstances when the spell is cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 07-21-2017, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T17:23:04-07:00","id":1119119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1118852-how-is-the-probability-for-fate-conditional-duration-evaluated?p=1118872#post1118872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think its ST fiat territory here. You just have to come up with what sounds the best between your group. If you cast the &quot;goes off if i am about to die&quot; before doing something suicidal then its probably common, if you cast it and then hide in a bunker like a hermit then its probably improbable. I think the attainment will have some metagame knowledge (ie the ST will probably know) and give its bonus based on what he thinks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is more or less what I figured, given that it is a Fate attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T17:36:31-07:00","id":1119122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1118852-how-is-the-probability-for-fate-conditional-duration-evaluated?p=1118895#post1118895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And on an even sider note, I'd personally ask for something a little more exact than &quot;about to die&quot;, just because I'd have a hard time arbitrating that. Are you &quot;about to die&quot; if you're hanging off a ledge? If someone throws a grenade that risks killing you, are you &quot;about to die&quot; when you take the damage, when the grenade explodes but before you're damaged, when it's thrown or even when the enemy makes the decision to throw a grenade? If you're infiltrating an enemy compound at great personal risk are you constantly about to die? I'd much prefer something like &quot;when targeted by an attack&quot; or &quot;when my health track is full&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually funny because I was going to ask how specific they could be. I assume the condition trigger needs to relate to a thing that has already happened (take damage, a gun is fired, a person speaks), rather than a supposed future state. Ergo, you could not be &quot;about to die&quot; all the time because you currently are not dying, and the moment you would be dying, you would have triggered the attainment to drop your Hung Spell and release your other spell. <br /> <br /> If you're hanging from a cliff, I don't believe it should trigger until you fall and take damage that may eventually kill you, or you die instantly and the abilities never go off.<br /> <br /> You could probably wrap the whole process in a Fate/Time spell to detect a failure-state in your immediate future and prompt your attainment to the condition of &quot;about to die.&quot;<br /> <br /> The more I think of it, even if you said &quot;end Hung Spell if my second-rightmost health box is about to take aggravated damage&quot;, you could still be killed or incapacitated without that ever even needing to happen. <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, it seems probability is pretty much in the hands of the ST's interpretation. That's cool.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}